fixture far_edge_landing_buffered_jump_keeps_stride
doc run right on test/ledge448, jump, air jump on tick 10, then hold jump from tick 28. Tick 35 comes down on the ledge's far edge and the buffered jump fires on that landing (BUILD.md s15 "Jump pressed 8 frames before landing fires on the landing frame"), from where the landing tick's whole step ends: the tick still carries the run's 9 u across, as every other landing tick does (physics review 5, M2).
room test/ledge448
spawn 322 448
frames 40
input
  0..3 R
  4..8 R jump
  9 R
  10..14 R jump
  15..27 R
  28..39 R jump
end
expect
  at 35 event.land=1 event.jump=1
  at 35 x>=8u+x@34
end
